    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11072": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice Campus: Florham Campus, Madison, NJ Department: School of Pharmacy and Health Sciences-Florham Hiring Manager: Ligia Westrich Hiring Manager Title: Assistant Dean, Academic Affairs College: Position Type: Faculty Grade: Faculty FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Assistant Professor Salary: $115,000--$130,000. General Benefits Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: Fairleigh Dickinson University College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences seeks applicants for a Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice within the Department of Pharmacy Practice (ambulatory/acute care clinical sites options may include Atlantic Medical Group, Hackensack-Meridian Health, or Valley Medical group ). The FDU College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences prepares pharmacists who will provide patient-centered care, advance the pharmacy profession through research and patient and public health advocacy, as well as serve as future health care leaders. FDU College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences offers an integrated curriculum that seeks to develop pharmacy practitioners who are able to effectively communicate with diverse populations and work as integral members of interprofessional health care teams. Further, the College offers a concurrent Master’s degree program to qualified pharmacy students. The clinical faculty position is a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure track appointment (rank and salary commensurate with skills and experience). Faculty members are expected to support the FDU College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences vision through teaching in the didactic and experiential professional pharmacy curriculum, developing a research agenda within their discipline and providing service to the College and University at large. This position will be affiliated with a clinical practice site that is seeking a clinical pharmacy practice faculty member to participate in direct patient care. It is expected that clinical assistant/associate professor will maintain active interdisciplinary practice at their assigned clinical site. Primary responsibilities of a faculty member at the clinical site will include educating Fairleigh Dickinson University students, residents (if applicable), and pharmacy staff, providing and documenting pharmacotherapeutic interventions/pharmacy consultations, attending interdisciplinary rounds (where applicable), providing patient counseling/medication reconciliation, documenting medication errors/adverse drug reactions, and participating in quality improvement initiatives as assigned by the director of pharmacy or clinical supervisor at the clinical site. Teaching in the didactic pharmacy curriculum, supporting student success initiatives, exam proctoring, committee engagement at the College, and participating in scholarly activities will also be expected. Required Qualifications: 1. Have a PharmD degree with a minimum of PGY -1 residency training ( PGY -2 preferred); 2. Demonstrate understanding of academic pharmacy, experiential education, and ACPE accreditation standards related to curriculum and experiential education; 3. Show a desire to participate in expanding new educational platforms, including integration of technology and active learning; 4. Demonstrate leadership and initiative in supporting School’s assessment and accreditation efforts; 5. Have a vision for the future of pharmacy education as a global enterprise; 6. Develop a personal philosophy and program of teaching, research and service focused on enriching students and enhancing the profession. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 10/09/2025 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/10861": {
      "title": "Asst/Assoc Professor, Pharmaceutical Sciences (pharmacology)",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Asst/Assoc Professor, Pharmaceutical Sciences (pharmacology) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Asst/Assoc Professor, Pharmaceutical Sciences (pharmacology) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Asst/Assoc Professor, Pharmaceutical Sciences (pharmacology) Campus: Florham Campus, Madison, NJ Department: Pharmacy-Florham Hiring Manager: Ligia Westrich Hiring Manager Title: Assistant Dean, Academic Affairs College: College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences Position Type: Faculty Grade: Faculty FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Assistant Professor Salary: $100,000-$121.540 General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: health/dental/RX/vision insurance, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: Fairleigh Dickinson University College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences invites applications for a 12-month, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in the Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences. The successful candidate will play a key role in the development and delivery of the Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) curriculum with a focus on pharmaceutical sciences. Teaching responsibilities include didactic courses in biomedical sciences (anatomy, physiology, pathophysiology), integrated pharmacotherapy (pharmacology portion), and other relevant areas within pharmaceutical sciences. A strong commitment to active learning, educational technology, and student success is essential. In addition to teaching, the faculty member is expected to maintain an active research and scholarly agenda in their area of expertise and to engage students in faculty-mentored research. Service on College and University committees is required and will be considered as part of the tenure evaluation process. College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences is located in Northern New Jersey. The College offers an integrated 4-year Pharm.D. curriculum. Further, a concurrent Master’s degree program is available to qualified pharmacy students. The mission of College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences is to create a values-based, student-centered learning experience that prepares graduates who are committed to improving the health of individuals and populations through leadership roles in pharmacy practice, health care research, and related health care fields. Our Doctor of Pharmacy program vision is to prepare future pharmacists for diverse roles across the health care continuum through a culture of learning, scholarship, innovation, advocacy, and leadership. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Required Qualifications: Education, training, experience: · A Ph.D. degree in Pharmaceutical Sciences is required. Understanding of pharmacy curriculum related to pharmaceutical sciences is required. A professional degree in pharmacy is a plus. · Faculty candidates specializing in pharmacology are especially encouraged to apply. · Teaching and research records will qualify the faculty candidate for the rank of assistant or associate professor. · Demonstrated experience and ability to adapt teaching to various learning styles and levels of learners are highly desirable. Successful applicants will: · Hold appropriate credentials and qualifications within their academic discipline. · Demonstrate a strong commitment to student engagement and a willingness to contribute to the development of innovative educational platforms. · Cultivate a personal philosophy and program of teaching, research, and service that enriches student learning and advances the pharmacy profession. · Maintain a research agenda that is feasible and well-aligned with the College’s existing research facilities and resources. · Collaborate effectively with practice faculty and colleagues across other healthcare disciplines in an interprofessional education environment. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates considered for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 03/10/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Research Statement Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
