    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11132": {
      "title": "Asst Director of Educational Opportunity Fund Program/Counselor/Recruitment Coordinator-Metro",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Asst Director of Educational Opportunity Fund Program/Counselor/Recruitment Coordinator-Metro Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Asst Director of Educational Opportunity Fund Program/Counselor/Recruitment Coordinator-Metro Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Asst Director of Educational Opportunity Fund Program/Counselor/Recruitment Coordinator-Metro Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Educational Opportunity Fund-Metro Hiring Manager: Lissette Garcia Hiring Manager Title: Executive Director, EOF College: Position Type: Professional Administrative Grade: 25 FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $56,139.-$62,418. General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: Under the direction of the Campus Director of the Educational Opportunity Fund Program, the incumbent is responsible for providing a comprehensive program for academically and financially disadvantaged students. Serving as a case manager to a cohort of students, the Assistant Director will provide academic, career, and financial advising to assigned students to ensure persistence to graduation. The incumbent will also manage all aspects of caseload needs, including providing programs, seminars, and workshops regarding adjustment and transition issues related to academic and student development, to enhance student success (persistence, retention, and performance). As Recruitment Coordinator, the incumbent will participate in all aspects of the admissions process as it relates to EOF recruitment. As Academic Coordinator, the incumbent will also oversee the academic component and provide academic support to all program participants. Required Qualifications: 1. Master’s Degree in Guidance/Counseling, Psychology, Education, or other appropriate academic disciplines. A Baccalaureate Degree and relevant experience may be substituted for the Master’s Degree. 2. A minimum of 2 years of relevant experience working with academically and economically disadvantaged students is preferred. 3. Experience in college recruitment, admission, advisement, and facilitating workshops, preferred. 4. Strong interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. 5. Experience in utilizing computer systems for word processing, data management, and other applications. 6. Must be available to work non-standard hours and have a flexible schedule as needed. 7. A valid driver’s license is required, and the ability to travel to off-site locations as needed. 8. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing background check. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 09/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
