    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11163": {
      "title": "Enrollment Services Specialist",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Enrollment Services Specialist Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Enrollment Services Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Enrollment Services Specialist Campus: Vancouver, British Columbia Canada Department: Enrollment and Student Services-Vancouver Hiring Manager: Arlette Hernandez Hiring Manager Title: Director of Enrollment Services College: Position Type: Staff Grade: FLSA: Non-Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: 49,000 - 59,000 CAD General Benefits Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: The Enrollment Services Specialist provides administrative and clerical support to the Offices of Enrollment Services.  Responsibilities include but are not limited to updating and filing of records and documents; assisting with the processing of student payments, deposits, and refunds; assisting students with online registration; assisting students with inquiries at the Enrollment Services Office; updating, generating and distribution of reports; proofreading of documents; and processing requests for transcripts and other documents. Supervision Received: The incumbents in this position are supervised by the Director of Enrollment Services.  Incumbents are required to follow and adhere to University and Office policy as established by the University. Required Qualifications: Principal Duties: 1.  Conducts Graduation Audits for eligible students and supports the Director of Enrollment Services in Commencement Planning. 2.  Responds to inquiries in person, by phone, and email; handles general office administration and filing of student/department records (electronic and paper). 3.  Processes ID cards for students, faculty, and staff, and updates student information (address, demographic, immigration, medical, etc.) in Colleague and other systems. 4.  Assists students with Web Advisor/Student Planning, online registration, and issues related to their academic program, escalating unresolved matters as needed. 5.  Supports Enrollment Services’ financial operations, including student billing, payments, refunds, and deposit processing during staff holidays. 6.  Manages document requests (transcripts, enrollment confirmations, graduation verifications) and updates transfer credit requests in the BCCAT database. 7.  Reviews Payment Deferment Plan requests and assists students missing transfer credits during admissions. 8.  Updates degree requirements in the Student Planning system, organizes student training sessions, and monitors academic plans. 9.  Updates information in the Robinson Student Information System and processes reports. 10.   Performs additional duties as assigned. Direction to Others: May participate in the training of new Enrollment Services employees. Standards: 1.  Knowledgeable of Enrollment Services policies, particularly registration and database maintenance. 2.  Strong communication skills and judgment when interacting with faculty, students, and staff. 3.  Able to work independently, manage multiple projects, and make decisions with discretion. 4.  Proficient in maintaining databases, drafting letters, handling complex calculations, and managing large sums of money per university procedures. 5.  Skilled in working with spreadsheets, organizing tasks, setting priorities, and managing time efficiently. 6.  Able to follow through on responsibilities and collaborate effectively with coworkers. Minimum Qualifications: 1.  High School diploma or GED required. 2.  At least 2 years of administrative experience in a fast-paced setting, ideally in academia, with budget management and basic accounting skills. 3.  Proficient in data management, Microsoft Office, and able to learn new applications quickly (Ellucian Colleague experience is a plus). 4.  Familiarity with college environments, either as a student or employee. 5.  Detail-oriented with strong organizational and communication skills. 6.  Must be available for overtime and non-standard hours (evenings, weekends). 7.  Canadian residency or work permit required, with background check upon hire. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 per week Posting Date: 09/03/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you legally eligible for employment in Canada?  Verification will be required upon employment. Yes No * Please indicate your Canadian employment status Canadian Citizen Permanent Resident Not Applicable Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11103": {
      "title": "FDU",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Admissions Officer - CRM Administrator (DBA) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Admissions Officer - CRM Administrator (DBA) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Admissions Officer - CRM Administrator (DBA) Campus: Vancouver, British Columbia Canada Department: Admissions, Vancouver Hiring Manager: Juliana Fiorentino Hiring Manager Title: Associate Director of Admissions College: No Response Position Type: Staff Grade: FLSA: Non-Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $60000 - $70000 CAD General Benefits Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: General Description: The Admissions Officer – CRM Administrator provides diversified administrative support to the Admissions Office. Responsibilities include overseeing the organizations data infrastructure for the transition to Slate CRM , be the Slate expert on campus and develop training and development for other staff and evaluating applications and responding to inquiries concerning undergraduate and graduate admissions. Supervision Received: This position is supervised by the Associate Director of Admissions and works closely with other departments related to their duties (i.e., Academic Advising, Recruitment, Marketing, Enrollment Services, and Faculty). Principal Duties: 1. Oversee the maintenance Slate to ensure it serves FDU Vancouver to better recruit and admit students 2. Understand organizational Slate needs and leverage the platforms functionality to enhance the recruitment and admission experience for both students and agents 3. Share relevant feedback with Slate development team and communicate relevant updates and functionality with staff and faculty 4. Process applications, acknowledges receipt of applications, produce student files and correlate transcripts and test scores with files in preparation for evaluation. Verify the authenticity of documents received from or on authorized behalf of applicants. 5. Provide outstanding customer service, maintaining contact with prospective students and applicants, including follow-up letters indicating the receipt of an application, incomplete applications (missing documents) and completed files. 6. Review transcripts, evaluate applicants’ academic record, calculate overall grade point averages, and determine the eligibility of an application to be considered for admission. 7. Make initial admission decisions to admit or refuse applicants to University programs based on established University guidelines. 8. Perform application reviews in CRM Recruit/Slate and export data into Ellucian Colleague database. 9. Monitor daily statistics of incoming applications help prioritize work for certain application types. 10. Generate decision letters and communication as directed by the Associate Director of Admissions. 11. Liaise with other departments to coordinate and support University events that relate to Admissions. 12. Recommend students who do not meet established prerequisites to Faculty Admissions Reviewing Committees and provide sufficient evidence of credentials to warrant a consideration for acceptance. 13. Research, review, and analyze admissions criteria from national and international institutions. 14. Perform other work-related admissions office related duties as assigned. Direction to Others: Provide Slate training to Admissions team members, and other internal stakeholders as necessary. Garner feedback from Slate users and share with necessary internal and external stakeholders. Required Qualifications: Standards: 1. Maintains knowledge of Admissions policies and procedures, and capable of communicating the same, particularly related to registration and database maintenance. 2. Capable of accurately maintaining student database. 3. Capable of personalizing form letters. 4. Capable of drafting forms and general information memos and letters. 5. Capable of working with and maintaining spreadsheets. 6. Capable of interacting successfully with the public under a variety of circumstances in a professional manner. 7. Must be able to follow through with responsibilities and interact effectively with co-workers. Preferred Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: 1. High School Diploma or GED required. 2. Completion of post-secondary courses related to office and business skills, or 2 years of experience in an office environment required. 3. Demonstrated knowledge of Slate CRM and how to effectively leverage this platform to optimize workflow for the recruitment and admissions experience for prospective students and agents. 4. Experience with computerized systems for data management, spreadsheet, word processing and e-mail applications. Knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. Ability to quickly learn new programs and applications. 5. Good human relations and communications skills, including telephone and typing skills. 6. Ability to handle multiple tasks simultaneously. 7. Strong proofreading skills. 8. Ability to take direction work collaboratively as a team player and be able to work independently. 9. Must be available to work overtime as required, including evenings and weekends. 10. Must be legally eligible to work in Canada. 11. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing a background check. Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 08/04/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you legally eligible for employment in Canada?  Verification will be required upon employment. Yes No Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Other Document Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
