se section is scheduled to be offered in-person in the FDU Metro campus. EGTC_1223 Introduction to CAD (2 Credits) Introduction to the practical use of computer hardware and software for drafting applications. This course includes 2 contact hours of lab and as such is a 4 contact hours course. Required Qualifications: Minimum qualification: A MS in Mechanical Engineering or other similar programs with experience in teaching college-level CAD course/s. Experience in AutoCAD is required. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check.  Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 04/16/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
