      "title": "Learning Disabilities Specialist-Part-time (General)",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Learning Disabilities Specialist-Part-time (General) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Learning Disabilities Specialist-Part-time (General) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Learning Disabilities Specialist-Part-time (General) Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Regional Center-Metro Hiring Manager: Dawn Dennis Hiring Manager Title: Campus Director College: Position Type: Professional Administrative Grade: 25 FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $33.00-$35.00 per hour General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, PTO , eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan (employer contributions may be available depending on length of service and hours worked), and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.). Status: Part-Time Months Worked: 9 Month Job Summary: Under the direction of the Campus Director, Regional Center for College Students with Learning Disabilities, the incumbent’s primary responsibilities will be clinical, involving the provision of diagnostic and academic support services to college students with learning disabilities. In addition, the Learning Disabilities Specialist ( LDS ) will be involved in assisting faculty in working with students and monitoring the student’s progress in their academic careers, gathering instructional resources and technological resources, and reviewing and entering data on the use of academic support. Required Qualifications: 1. Master’s degree in Learning Disabilities, Special Education or a related academic discipline is preferred. 2. A bility to support college level Math is required. 3. Three years Math teaching experience, preferably with secondary level students with learning disabilities. 4. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 14 hours per week Posting Date: Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
