    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/10592": {
      "title": "School of Education Clinical Supervisor-Part-time--Independent Consultant Position",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | School of Education Clinical Supervisor-Part-time--Independent Consultant Position Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions School of Education Clinical Supervisor-Part-time--Independent Consultant Position Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: School of Education Clinical Supervisor-Part-time--Independent Consultant Position Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: School of Education-Metro Hiring Manager: Kathryn Spence Hiring Manager Title: Director, School of Education College: Maxwell Becton College of Liberal Arts and Education Position Type: Faculty Grade: Faculty FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: No Response Salary: $135.00/Observation General Benefits n/a Status: Part-Time Months Worked: Job Summary: Fairleigh Dickinson University is seeking experienced educators to serve as clinical supervisors for graduate students in School of Education programs. For the fall semester, this role will support either paraprofessionals participating in FDU’s PARE (Paraprofessional Alternate Route Educators) Grant Program or Reading Specialists employed in schools throughout New Jersey. PARE Program Supervisors will support paraprofessionals in Bergen County, New Jersey transitioning into certified teaching roles by providing mentorship, observation, and evaluation during their clinical practicum placements. Supervisors will serve as liaisons between FDU and partnering schools, ensuring alignment between university expectations and school-based practices. Supervisors will conduct observations using FDU approved inventories. This is a meaningful opportunity to contribute to the development of future educators. Key Responsibilities Observe and evaluate paraprofessional teacher or Reading Specialist candidates during their practicum placements. Conduct goal-setting, pre-observation, and post-observation conferences at least every other week during the semester ( PARE ) or three times during the semester (Reading Specialist). Provide timely, constructive written and verbal feedback. Collaborate regularly with cooperating teachers and school personnel. Submit observation reports, competency inventories, and final evaluations using FDU’s data management system. Attend required orientations, training sessions, and supervisor meetings. Communicate consistently with the Director of Field Placement and respective graduate program directors regarding candidate progress and concerns. Support candidates in integrating university curriculum with school-based practices. Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in Education or a closely related field. Minimum of 5 years of teaching or administrative experience. Demonstrated expertise in mentoring or supervising educators. Experience working in urban or underserved school settings. Strong communication and organizational skills. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and equitable learning environment Preferred Qualifications: Experience supervising paraprofessionals or non-traditional teacher candidates. Familiarity with remote teaching tools and practices. Prior involvement in grant-funded educational programs. Hours Worked Posting Date: 09/05/2025 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Other Document Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/10987": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor for the PA Program (Clinical Phase) -Part-time",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Clinical Assistant Professor for the PA Program (Clinical Phase) -Part-time Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Clinical Assistant Professor for the PA Program (Clinical Phase) -Part-time Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor for the PA Program (Clinical Phase) -Part-time Campus: Florham Campus, Madison, NJ Department: Physician Assistant-Florham Hiring Manager: Dina Prisco Hiring Manager Title: Assistant Dean, Academic Affairs College: College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences Position Type: Faculty Grade: Faculty FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Clinical Rank Salary: $50,000 General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: Eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan, and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.), and State benefits such as NJ Sick Leave and State Short Term Disability benefits. Status: Part-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: Participates in the coordination the Clinical Phase (Professional Year II) of the PA Program, provides instruction and analyzes students’ performance and overall program outcomes for the Clinical Phase. DUTIES / RESPONSIBILITIES : 1. Participates in the coordination of Supervised Clinical Practice Experiences in the Clinical Phase of the PA Program. 2. Actively participates in the processes of designing, implementing, coordinating, and evaluating the curriculum (A2.05g) preparing syllabi for all courses in the Clinical Phase of the program. 3. Assists in the analysis of supervised clinical practice experiences for appropriateness of settings, patient demographics, types of patient interactions and diagnoses. 4. Assists in the scheduling of required and elective supervised clinical experiences. 5. Provides student instruction for an equivalent of one-two courses workload per semester (A2.05c). 6. Prepares and reviews exams, collaborates with faculty in test construction. Participates in the analysis of item performance and overall test construction. 7. Evaluates student performance (A2.05d) and monitors progress. 8. Assists in the analysis of clinical curriculum outcomes. 9. Assists in the analysis of student evaluations of rotations and preceptors. 10. Actively participates in the process of selecting applicants for admission to the PA Program (A2.05b). 11. Participates in clinical site visits as assigned. 12. Actively participates in the remediation process of students of remedial instruction, when needed (A2.05f). 13. Serves as a faculty advisor for PA students, meets with students, provides counseling, and assures appropriate intervention, when required. (A2.05e). 14. Attends and participates in PA committee meetings, program activities, and campus events. 15. Actively participates in the process of developing, reviewing and revising (as necessary) the mission statement, goals, and competencies (A2.05a) of the program. 16. Serves as a member of committees, assisting with preparing minutes and outcome reports. 17. Contributes to ongoing self-study process, evaluation of the program (A2.05h) and formal report to ARC -PA. 18. Serves as faculty leader for service-learning events. 19. Attends professional conferences, representing the PA Program and the University. Required Qualifications: Work Experience: Minimum 3-5 years clinical experience Academic experience (preferred) Education: Graduate of an ARC -PA accredited PA Program Masters degree (MS, MPA , MPH ), Doctorate preferred CERRTIFICATION / LICENSURER NCCPA Certification Licensed as a PA SPECIAL CONSIDERATIONS : 1 day a week dedicated to Clinical Practice or Research Available weekends for Campus Events (e.g., Campus Visit Days) Available evenings for program events (e.g., Research Forums) Note: As per the 5th edition of the ARC -PA Standards (effective September 2020), two principal faculty members must be hired by the institution on a permanent basis at least 9 months prior to the date of the scheduled site visit (D1.01c). Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 28 hours Posting Date: 07/14/2025 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
