      "title": "Coordinator of Disability Support Services (Florham Campus)",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Coordinator of Disability Support Services (Florham Campus) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Coordinator of Disability Support Services (Florham Campus) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Coordinator of Disability Support Services (Florham Campus) Campus: Florham Campus, Madison, NJ Department: Disability Support Services-Florham Hiring Manager: Pamela Cavanagh Hiring Manager Title: Director, Academic Support and Disability Support Services College: Position Type: Professional Administrative Grade: 23 FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $50,000 to $53,000 General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: The Coordinator of Disability Support Services reports to the Director of Disability Support and Academic Support Center and has responsibility for coordinating accommodations and related services for students with disabilities, managing the Office for Disability Support Services, supervising student personnel, and serving as a resource to the Fairleigh Dickinson University community. Additional responsibilities may be assigned by the Director. Required Qualifications: 1. Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree in Psychology, Special Education, Student Services Administration, Higher Education Administration, Management, or other field preferred. 2. A minimum of 1-year of related experience, including but not limited to: legal issues, higher education, and support services. 3. Familiarity with federal, state and local laws regarding access for people with disabilities preferred. 4. Strong oral and written communications and interpersonal skills. 5. Administrative experience which includes decision making and policy making. 6. Ability to work effectively with a diverse population of students, faculty, staff and administrators. 7. Knowledge of assistive technology software(s), strong computer skills, research and statistical reporting skills preferred. 8. Willing and able to work non-standard hours as required, including evenings and weekends 9. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Monday- Friday 9 am to 5 pm (may need to work on some weekends depending on university events) Posting Date: 09/03/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/10732": {
      "title": "Network Analyst and Student Intern Coordinator",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Network Analyst and Student Intern Coordinator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Network Analyst and Student Intern Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Network Analyst and Student Intern Coordinator Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Information Resources & Technology-Metro Hiring Manager: Stuart Alper Hiring Manager Title: AVP, Systems and Network College: Position Type: Professional Administrative Grade: 27 FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $54,900.-$87,800. General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: Under the direction of the Director of Networking, the Network Analyst and Student Intern Coordinator implements, maintains, assists in planning and troubleshoots network/telecommunications equipment. The incumbent may also be called upon to install, maintain and support software utilities and applications associated with the main Cisco networking systems and the telecommunications (voice/video/data) environment on an as needed basis as determined by the Director of Networking. This position is expected to assist in maintaining 7 day by 24-hour up time for all critical network segments. Required Qualifications: PRINCIPAL DUTIES : Network Analyst 80% of Resource 1. Installs, maintains and troubleshoots mostly Cisco Local Area Network ( LAN ) hardware and Wireless Access Points, primarily layer 2 switches. Also includes physical fiber/copper troubleshooting, patching and running. Some OSI layer 3 work and higher as the individual’s skill set permits. Maintains detailed documentation concerning layouts and connections. 2. Installs, maintains and troubleshoots LAN software, including operating systems, applications, utilities and management software. 3. Designs and conducts tests for monitoring and evaluating the continuing performance of all network equipment, including utilization, loading and response. Provides management reports showing the status of the environment. 4. Maintains a working knowledge of continuing developments in the field of Networking. Must make design and hardware recommendations to the Director of Networking. 5. On call 24 hours per day, 7 days per week. Required to work on weekends and holidays when scheduled. 6. Monitors and responses to end user tickets through the Ticket Management system. 7. Performs other work related duties as requested. PRINCIPAL DUTIES : Student Intern Coordinator: 20% of Resource 1. Assists with on-boarding training of each new wave of student Interns. 2. Works side-by-side with students on designated day to observe their work. 3. Meets with Interns 1:1 on a weekly basis to discuss training, skills learned, tickets processed, questions and ongoing improvements. 4. Works with Students on developing Knowledge Items and working with Auto Pilot call configurations. 5. Acts as primary mentor for Students working with faculty to ensure accreditation of program; recommend grades to faculty. 6. Serves as primary contact in the recruitment of Student Interns, including posting waves on Handshake and interviewing candidates. 7. Acts as liaison between Service Desk and Computer Science Department in management of Internship program. 8. Actively recruits new students to the program through promotions, presentations, etc. 9. Additional Service Desk hours must be approved by Director of Networking. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS : 1. Minimum of BS in Computer Science required plus two years of experience in Networking Technology. 2. Ability to demonstrate a strong working knowledge of Cisco IOS . Most importantly, around layer 2 configuration, ASIC based QOS , 802.1q, etherchannel, and spanning tree. Strong knowledge of IP subnetting, routing and VLAN’s. 3. Demonstrated aptitude in network management with experience in LAN , WAN , Wireless and VOIP technologies. 4. Thorough working knowledge of TCP /IP. 5. Past experience using network troubleshooting/certification devices such as a packet sniffer, OTDR , CATx certification tool or a wireless spectrum analyzer. 6. Ability to perform skilled work in the installation, maintenance and troubleshooting of networking/telecommunications equipment. 7. Effective organizational skills to meet schedules and timelines. 8. Ability to self-educate. Our environment is fast paced. Learning on your own rapidly and having the ability to produce are essential to success in this position. 9. Ability to communicate well orally and in writing. 10. Ability to communicate and interact with all levels of university personnel and students. 11. Ability to lift and carry equipment and supplies. 12. Valid driver’s license and accessibility to a car 24 hours per day, 7 days per week to accomplish support on any campus. 13. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 12/01/2025 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
