    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11155": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant for the School of Education-Part-time",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Administrative Assistant for the School of Education-Part-time Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Administrative Assistant for the School of Education-Part-time Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Administrative Assistant for the School of Education-Part-time Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: School of Education-Metro Hiring Manager: Kathryn Spence Hiring Manager Title: Director, School of Education College: Maxwell Becton College of Liberal Arts and Education Position Type: Staff Grade: 11 FLSA: Non-Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $22.44 -- $28.33 Hourly General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, PTO , eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan (employer contributions may be available depending on length of service and hours worked), and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.). Status: Part-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: The Administrative Assistant for the School of Education provides advanced and diversified administrative support services for the Office of the Director, assigned Program Director(s), and faculty of the SOE graduate programs. Major responsibilities include providing administrative assistance in supporting the SOE in the growth and development of its various graduate programs and initiatives for FDU graduate online programs, all NJ, and international campuses, as well as its off-campus programs in local school districts and communities. Additional responsibilities involve administrative support for course scheduling; faculty and student records; faculty advisement scheduling; purchasing; ordering supplies/resource materials; and data management, analysis, and reporting. Required Qualifications: 1. High School degree or GED required. College credits preferred. 2. A minimum of 3 years administrative work experience required, preferably in a multi-faceted, fast-paced work environment, including office oversight responsibilities, and interfacing with multiple organizational units. 3. Experience and a high level of proficiency related to the use of diverse technologies, data processing, data analysis, and reporting; and applications to tasks using word processing, database, spreadsheets, graphics, on-line services, and social media platforms, etc. 4. Advanced proficiency in the Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and custom database systems, with specific expertise in executing complex workflows like mail merges. Demonstrated ability to process, analyze, and report data, alongside a proven track record of quickly mastering new technologies. 5. Strong written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills, problem-solving ability, and organizational skills. 6. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 28 Weekly Posting Date: 08/20/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
