    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11047": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of Physics---Metro-2026",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Adjunct Professor of Physics---Metro-2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Adjunct Professor of Physics---Metro-2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Adjunct Professor of Physics---Metro-2026 Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Department of Chemistry, Biochemistry, and Physics-Metro Hiring Manager: James Dougherty Hiring Manager Title: Chair, Department  Biochemistry, Chemistry, and Physics College: Gregory H. Olsen College of Engineering and Science Position Type: Faculty Grade: Adjunct FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Adjunct Faculty Salary: $900.00-$1,000 per contract hour General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: Eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan, and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.), and State benefits such as NJ Sick Leave and State Short Term Disability benefits. Status: Temporary Months Worked: No Response Job Summary: The Department of Biochemistry, Chemistry, and Physics of the Gregory H. Olsen College of Engineering and Science at Fairleigh Dickinson University is seeking to hire adjuncts to teach physics lecture and/or lab sections on the Metro campus during the summer sessions as well as the academic calendar year. These sections meet in person and are scheduled to meet during the day and/or the evening. Responsibilities · Provide quality instruction* for undergraduate STEM students · Guide students through the performance of weekly physics lectures and/or laboratory experiments. · Evaluate student progress and provide appropriate feedback in a timely manner · Hold regular office hours · Track student attendance · Submit attendance verification, midterm grades and final grades online · Reply to emails from students, lab coordinators, and administrators in a timely manner · Commit to contributing to an inclusive working and learning environment · Follow established teaching protocols within the physics program *Quality instruction includes, but is not limited to, arriving on time and prepared to engage students through evidence-based active learning pedagogies, and/or assisting students with data collection and analysis via thoughtful guidance and encouragement. Required Qualifications: A minimum of a master’s degree (or equivalent) in Physics or a closely related field is required. Preference will be given to applicants with previous teaching experience. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae/resume. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 04/23/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
