    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/11159": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President for Finance",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Associate Vice President for Finance Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Associate Vice President for Finance Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Associate Vice President for Finance Campus: Metropolitan Campus, Teaneck, NJ Department: Financial Affairs, VP's Office-Metro Hiring Manager: Lisa Clarke Hiring Manager Title: Interim Vice President for Finance College: Position Type: Professional Administrative Grade: 34 FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Salary: $160,000--$180,000 General Benefits This position provides a comprehensive benefits package that includes: employee tuition grant, health/dental/RX/vision insurance, paid time off, retirement plan contributions, employer paid life insurance and long term disability benefits, as well as various voluntary benefits including but not limited to supplemental life insurance, commuter benefits, long term care, and FSA / HSA . Status: Full-Time Months Worked: 12 Month Job Summary: Reporting to the Vice President for Finance and Treasurer, the Associate Vice President for Finance serves as the senior operational leader for the Finance Division and is responsible for the effective day-to-day management of the University’s accounting, financial reporting, budgeting, purchasing/procurement, audit coordination, tax and regulatory compliance, and related finance operations. The Associate Vice President translates institutional financial strategy into disciplined processes, reliable forecasts, timely reporting, strong internal controls, and effective financial management across the University. The position works closely with the Vice President for Finance and Treasurer to implement the annual budget, long-range financial plan, scenario analyses, and the financial components of strategic initiatives and partnerships. In a challenging higher education environment, the Associate Vice President is expected to be a hands-on leader who strengthens accountability, develops staff, improves processes and systems, and provides responsive, decision-useful financial support while maintaining appropriate stewardship and control. Required Qualifications: 1. Bachelor’s degree required in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a closely related field. CPA certification required; Master’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related field preferred. 2. Minimum of eight years of progressively responsible accounting, budgeting, financial reporting, or financial management experience required, including significant supervisory or management responsibility. Experience in higher education, a not-for-profit organization, or public accounting serving complex not-for-profit or higher education clients strongly preferred. 3. Demonstrated knowledge of generally accepted accounting principles, financial statement preparation, audit requirements, internal controls, budgeting, forecasting, cash management, tax and regulatory compliance, and financial reporting in a complex organization. 4. Demonstrated ability to manage an annual budget process, develop forecasts and financial models, analyze variances and trends, and translate financial information into practical recommendations for operating leaders. 5. Demonstrated success improving financial processes, controls, reporting, and systems. Experience with enterprise financial systems, preferably Ellucian, and advanced proficiency with Excel and financial reporting/analytics tools required. 6. Strong leadership, communication, and management skills, including the ability to develop staff, establish accountability, manage competing priorities, and work effectively with diverse academic and administrative constituencies in a resource-constrained and changing environment. 7. Ability to comprehend, interpret, and apply policies, procedures, laws, regulations, accounting standards, and institutional guidelines; ability to identify risk and exercise sound judgment in complex situations. 8. Ability to handle matters of a highly confidential and sensitive nature with discretion, professionalism, and sound judgment. 9. Valid driver’s license and accessibility to transportation for travel between campuses. 10. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked 35 Posting Date: 09/11/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.fdu.edu/postings/10746": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of Sociology--Spring 2026",
      "description": "FDU - Job Site | Adjunct Professor of Sociology--Spring 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FDU Home Page HR Home Page Benefits Clery Act Information For Faculty and Staff Metropolitan Campus Map/Directions Florham Campus Map/Directions Vancouver Campus Map/Directions Adjunct Professor of Sociology--Spring 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details (Default Section) Job Title: Adjunct Professor of Sociology--Spring 2026 Campus: Florham Campus, Madison, NJ Department: Social Sciences & History-Florham Hiring Manager: Robert Houle Hiring Manager Title: Chair College: Maxwell Becton College of Liberal Arts and Education Position Type: Faculty Grade: Adjunct FLSA: Exempt Faculty Rank: Adjunct Faculty Salary: $1,150.credit hour General Benefits This position provides a benefits package that includes: Eligibility to contribute towards the 403(b) plan, and a various fringe benefits (discounts on ever day good and services, entertainment/dining discounts, etc.), and State benefits such as NJ Sick Leave and State Short Term Disability benefits. Status: Temporary Months Worked: No Response Job Summary: The Department of Social Sciences, History, and Criminal Justice (part of the Maxwell Becton College of Arts and Sciences) at Fairleigh Dickinson University ( https://www.fdu.edu/ ) is looking for part-time (adjunct) faculty to teach sections of Sociology starting in Spring 2026. Sections are 3 credit hours and meet Monday-Thursday, Tuesday-Friday, or as a double block on different days including Wednesday. At this time, we are looking for someone to teach two sections of Introduction to Sociology. Required Qualifications: The ideal candidate would have a Ph.D. in Sociology. We will be happy to consider you if you have an advanced degree in Sociology and/or are an advanced graduate school student with teaching experience in a University setting. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statements of research interests and teaching interests/philosophy, as well as the names and contact information of three references. Questions? Email Chris Sobczak (c.sobczak@fdu.edu), Administrative Assistant of Social Sciences, History, and Criminal Justice. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check and produce a Social Security Card. Preferred Qualifications: Hours Worked Posting Date: 12/15/2025 Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Types Accepted: Application for Employment, Faculty Profile Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Other Document Footer goes here To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
